@startuml
title Cookies: Export, Upload and Use
skinparam shadowing false

start
:User exports cookies.txt outside the app\n(browser extension, or scripts/export_cookies_via_cdp.py);
:Upload it in the analyzer panel\n(or place it at data/cookies.txt);
if (cookies file exists?) then (yes)
  :Pass data/cookies.txt to yt-dlp;
else (no)
  :Run unauthenticated;
endif

if (YouTube requires login/bot check?) then (yes)
  :Return ONE actionable error:/nexport cookies.txt and upload it;
  note right
    The app never reads a browser profile.
    Edge cookies are v20 app-bound encrypted
    (undecryptable offline), and the old
    fallback closed every Edge window.
    See ai/bug-fix/038.
  end note
  stop
else (no)
  :Continue normally;
endif

stop
@enduml
